W: Refrain:
W:
W: Lully, lulla, thou little tiny child.
W: Bye, bye, lully, lullay, thou little tiny child.
W: Bye, bye, lully, lullay.
W:
W: 1. O sisters two,
W: How may we do
W: For to preserve this day
W: This poor youngling
W: For whom we do sing
W: Bye, bye, lully lullay.
W: (Refrain:)
W:
W: 2. Herod the king,
W: In his raging,
W: Chargèd he hath this day
W: His men of might,
W: In his own sight
W: All young children to slay.
W: (Refrain:)
W:
W: 3. That woe is me,
W: Poor child, for thee,
W: And ever mourn and say:
W: For thy parting
W: Neither say nor sing
W: Bye, bye, lully lullay.
W: (Refrain:)
W: %
